I approved slate v2 for H1388 under the mandate, and the target is now at **APPROVED**.

**The check:**
- **Gates:** all five models pass all four pocket gates (complete, phospho_pocket, motif, assembled). I checked each one in `gates/pocket_A1B1.csv`.
- **Model 1** (`A1B1__sep__af3__s20_0`) is the top-ranked AF3 model with the phosphoserine at peptide position 7 (pS7). Its ranking score is 0.963 and its ipTM 0.939, and pS7 sits 2.5 Å from the 14-3-3 gamma phosphate pocket (K49/R56/R131/Y132).
- **Against the decisions:** the slate has nothing that contradicts them.
  - All five are the one-peptide, one-protomer complex (A1B1), as D2 decided.
  - AF3 with pS7 leads with three different seeds (s20, s9, s7).
  - Two Protenix models (s5, s10) put the peptide core in the same position, within 0.5 Å of the agreed pose, as D7 and the results checkpoint (C2) chose.
- **Files:** all five model files are there, 154–164 kB each.
- **No grounds for NEEDS HUMAN:** model 1 passes every gate and the slate matches D2 and D5–D7.

**One thing to know:** the two Protenix models carry plain serine at position 7, not phosphoserine, because Protenix did not write the modification into its output. This was already known. The plan checkpoint allowed unmodified models on the slate as long as they pass the gates (C1 Q4a), and both do.

**On record:**
- The check is saved as evidence `slate_approval_check`.
